{
  "$comment": [
    "The view register for the data-arrival tier (#746).",
    "",
    "scripts/check-arrival-coverage.sh enumerates every view from the product",
    "itself — dashboard tabs from VALID_TABS in DashboardHtml.ts, webview panels",
    "from the createWebviewPanel() call sites under src/, tree views from",
    "package.json's contributes.views — and requires each to appear here exactly",
    "once. Adding a view therefore cannot be done silently: the guard fails until",
    "the view is either given an arrival test or explicitly recorded as pending.",
    "",
    "A `dashboard-tab` entry may NOT be pending. Those are the surfaces epic #741",
    "found broken, and this issue's slice covers all thirteen.",
    "",
    "`arrivalTest` names the file, and `marker` the string that file must contain",
    "(`arrival:<id>`) — so deleting or renaming the tests for one view fails the",
    "guard instead of leaving a registry entry pointing at a file that no longer",
    "covers it."
  ],
  "views": [
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "kind": "dashboard-tab",
      "transport": "local telemetry (JSONL) + platform.getUsageSummary",
      "arrivalTest": "tests/arrival/dashboardLocalTabs.test.ts",
      "failureFidelity": true
    },
    {
      "id": "pipeline",
      "kind": "dashboard-tab",
      "transport": "local telemetry (JSONL) + PipelineStateService events",
      "arrivalTest": "tests/arrival/dashboardLocalTabs.test.ts",
      "failureFidelity": false,
      "note": "No failure kind exists for a local read beyond 'no runs yet', which the History empty-state test covers."
    },
